 📌 Overview

The Shopify Product Taxonomy Classification System is a Django-based platform that automatically analyzes product catalogues and assigns products to the most 
appropriate Shopify Product Taxonomy category.

The system accepts product data from Excel/CSV catalogues, processes product titles, descriptions, materials, and other available attributes, and uses a TF-IDF + cosine 
similarity classification engine to identify suitable taxonomy categories.

Each prediction includes:

* 🎯 Predicted taxonomy category
* 📊 Confidence score
* 🔀 Alternative category suggestions
* 🏷️ Extracted product attributes
* 🖼️ Image URL validation status
* 👤 Manual review status

For large catalogues, classification is processed asynchronously using Celery + Redis, allowing the web application to remain responsive while thousands of products are processed in the background.



 🎯 Problem Statement

Large e-commerce catalogues often contain thousands of products with inconsistent or incomplete category information.

Manually categorizing every product can be:

* Time-consuming
* Difficult to maintain consistently
* Expensive at scale
* Prone to human error

This system provides an automated first-pass classification pipeline while keeping human reviewers in the loop for uncertain predictions.

# Example

Input

text
Product Name:
Men's Waterproof Running Shoes

Description:
Lightweight men's running shoes with waterproof mesh,
rubber outsole and cushioned sole.


Classification

text
Predicted Category:
Apparel & Accessories > Shoes > Athletic Shoes

Confidence:
0.91

Alternative Suggestions:
1. Shoes > Running Shoes
2. Shoes > Outdoor Shoes
3. Shoes > Casual Shoes

Review Status:
AI Approved / Pending Review




# ✨ Features

# 📥 Product Catalogue Import

* Import products from Excel/CSV files
* Handles large catalogues
* Validates product rows before processing
* Gracefully handles missing or incomplete data

# 🧠 AI-Assisted Classification

Uses a lightweight and explainable NLP pipeline:

text
Product Title
      +
Description
      +
Available Attributes
      ↓
Text Preprocessing
      ↓
TF-IDF Vectorization
      ↓
Cosine Similarity
      ↓
Shopify Taxonomy Matching


No GPU or large training dataset is required.

# 📊 Confidence Scoring

Each classification produces a numerical confidence score.

Example:

text
Category: Athletic Shoes
Confidence: 0.91


Low-confidence classifications can automatically be sent for human review.

# 🔀 Alternative Suggestions

When the prediction is uncertain, the system provides the top alternative categories.

text
Prediction
───────────
1. Athletic Shoes     0.91
2. Running Shoes      0.84
3. Outdoor Shoes      0.78


This helps reviewers make corrections quickly.

# 🏷️ Attribute Detection

Automatically extracts useful product attributes such as:

* Color
* Material
* Assembly Required
* Product Type
* Other supported attributes

# 🖼️ Image Validation

Product image URLs are checked automatically to identify:

* Missing image URLs
* Invalid URLs
* Broken/unreachable images
* Failed image requests

Image validation can be executed independently from classification.

# 👥 Role-Based Access

The application separates responsibilities between:

Admin

* Import catalogues
* Start classification jobs
* Monitor processing
* Manage products
* View classification results

Reviewer

* View uncertain classifications
* Review AI predictions
* Approve classifications
* Manually correct categories

# ⚡ Asynchronous Processing

Large classification jobs run in the background using:

text
Django
   │
   ├── Creates Classification Job
   │
   ▼
Celery
   │
   ▼
Redis
   │
   ▼
Celery Worker
   │
   ▼
Classification Engine
   │
   ▼
MariaDB


The user does not have to keep the browser request open while thousands of products are being processed.

# 🔁 Resumable Classification

Classification is designed to continue from unprocessed records.

If a worker stops during a large batch:

text
10,000 products
      ↓
Processed: 6,500
      ↓
Worker interrupted
      ↓
Restart worker
      ↓
Continue remaining products


Previously processed products are not unnecessarily reprocessed.

# 🔌 REST API

Django REST Framework provides API endpoints for:

* Listing classifications
* Viewing individual results
* Approving classifications
* Updating classification data
* Pagination

# 🛡️ Fault-Tolerant Processing

Individual bad records should not terminate the entire batch.

The pipeline handles cases such as:

* Missing product descriptions
* Empty fields
* Invalid rows
* Broken image URLs
* Unexpected input values



