# 🧠 Classification Pipeline

The classification process follows these steps:

text
1. Import Product Catalogue
             ↓
2. Validate Product Data
             ↓
3. Combine Relevant Text Fields
             ↓
4. Preprocess Text
             ↓
5. Generate TF-IDF Vectors
             ↓
6. Compare Against Taxonomy
             ↓
7. Calculate Similarity Scores
             ↓
8. Select Best Category
             ↓
9. Generate Alternative Categories
             ↓
10. Extract Product Attributes
             ↓
11. Validate Product Images
             ↓
12. Save Classification Result
             ↓
13. Flag Low-Confidence Results
             ↓
14. Human Review & Approval




# 📊 Classification Result

A typical classification result contains:

| Field              | Description                     |
|  | - |
| Product            | Original product                |
| Predicted Category | Selected taxonomy category      |
| Confidence         | Classification confidence score |
| Alternatives       | Other suitable categories       |
| Attributes         | Extracted product attributes    |
| Image Status       | Image URL validation result     |
| Review Status      | Pending / Approved / Corrected  |
| Reviewer           | User who reviewed the result    |



